# promise: #356
# Tabs picked with ⌘/⇧-click get Arc's menu for all of them at once: Copy URLs puts every link on
# the clipboard, one per line and without trackers (as ⇧⌘C does), and Share N Items hands them all
# to the Mac's share services. The menu is the one a right-click on a picked row builds; Today
# lists the newest tab first.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=one
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=two%26utm_source=x
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=three
wait 2
cra://debug?pickedMenu=2&label=two
expect-log picked menu two: Open in Split View\|Duplicate\|──\|Copy URLs\|Share 2 Items ▸\|──\|Move to Space ▸\|New Folder with 2 Items\|──\|Change Icon \(off\)\|Mute\|──\|Close 2 Tabs\|Deselect All$
cra://debug?pickedMenu=3&label=copy&run=Copy URLs
expect-log picked menu copy ran Copy URLs: \S*n=three⏎\S*n=two⏎\S*n=one picks=3$
